WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.810
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:11.120
Today we are going to control the fate of
liquids in virtual worlds.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.250
This footage is from one of my earlier papers
where I attempted fluid control.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.030
This means that we are not only simulating
the movement of a piece of fluid, but we wish

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.850
to coerce it to flow into a prescribed shape.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:31.760
This was super challenging and I haven’t
really seen a satisfactory solution that I

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.440
think, artist could use in the industry yet.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.620
And now that we have these modern, neural-network
based algorithms, we are now able to solve

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.789
problems that we never even dreamed of solving
just a few years ago.

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:51.289
For instance, they can already perform this
kind of style transfer for smoke simulations.

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.129
Which is, incredible.

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:56.699
So, are you thinking what I am thinking?

00:00:56.699 --> 00:01:00.170
Can one of those maybe tackle fluid control
too?

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.780
Well, that’s a tough call… just to showcase
how difficult this problem is.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:11.600
If we wish to have any control over our fluid
simulations, if we are a trained artist, we

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.049
can sculpt the fluid directly ourselves.

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:20.759
Of course, this requires a great deal of expertise,
and often, hours of work.

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:22.630
Can we do better?

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.130
Well, yes, kind of.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:31.100
We can use a particle system built into most
modern 3D modeling programs, with which we

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.570
can try to guide these particles to a given
direction.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:40.539
This took about 20 minutes, and it still requires
some artistic expertise.

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:43.359
So, that’s it then?

00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:47.210
No, hold on to your papers, and check this
out!

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.240
The preparation for this work takes place
in virtual reality, where we can make these

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.439
sketches in 3D, and look at that!

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:00.219
The liquid magically takes the shape of our
sketch.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.490
So, how long did this take?

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.630
Well, not one hour, and not even 20 minutes.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.340
It took one minute.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.369
One minute.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:11.900
Now we’re talking!

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.400
And even better, we can embed this into a
simulation, and it will behave like a real

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.270
piece of fluid should.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:22.250
So, what is all this good for?

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:28.780
Well, my experience has been in computer graphics
is that if we put a powerful tool like this

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.909
into the hands of capable artist, they are
going to create things that we never even

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:35.850
thought of creating.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.660
With this, they can make a heart from wine.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.890
Or create a milky skirt.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.989
Several variants even, if we wish.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:46.959
Or a liquid butterfly.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:53.540
I am loving these solutions, and don’t forget,
all of these can be then embedded into a virtual

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.480
world and simulated as a real liquid.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:03.750
Now, we talked about three solutions, and
how much they take, but we didn’t see what

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.810
they looked like.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:11.860
Clearly, it is hard to compare these mathematically,
so this is going to be, of course, subjective.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.200
So, this took an hour.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:19.970
It looks very smooth, and is perhaps the most
beautiful of the three solutions.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.340
That is great.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.549
However, as a drawback, it does not look like
a real-world water splash.

00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:32.860
The particle system took 20 minutes, it creates
a more lifelike version of our letter, but

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.150
the physics is still missing.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.970
This still looks like a trail of particles,
not a physics system.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.319
And, let’s see the new method.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:47.200
Yes, this took only a minute, and it finally
looks like a real splash.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:53.230
Now, make no mistake, all three of these solutions
can be excellent, depending on our artistic

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.230
vision.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.250
So, how does all this magic happen?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.810
What is the architecture of this neural network?

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:06.670
Well, this behavior emerges not from one,
but from the battle of two neural networks.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:13.849
A generator neural network creates new splashes,
and the discriminator finds out whether these

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:16.970
splashes are real or fake.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:22.450
Over time, they challenge each other, and
they teach each other to do better.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:26.250
The technique also goes the extra mile beyond
just sketching.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:30.390
Look, for instance, your brush strokes can
also describe velocities.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:37.380
With this, we can not only control the shape,
but even the behavior of the fluid too.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.690
So, there we go.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:45.260
Finally, a learning-based technique gives
us a proper solution for fluid control.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:51.500
And here comes the best part - is it not only
quicker than previous solutions, it can also

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.510
be used by anyone.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:56.410
No artistic expertise is required!

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:26.020
What a time 

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:35.490
to be alive!

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:45.360
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

